1.1.text:
Article 3
The implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence, is carried out based on the following principles:
a. respect for Human Rights possessed by women and children;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination; and
d. the best interests of women and children. Article 4 The purpose and objectives of implementing protection for women and children from acts of violence, include:
a. prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children;
b. handling services, assistance and recovery for women and children who become victims of acts of violence;
c. reunification; and
d. empowerment of women and rehabilitation of children who become victims of acts of violence.

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE MAYOR OF BITUNG,

Considering : a. that the guarantee of respect, protection and fulfillment of Human Rights for every Indonesian Citizen in the Region is a duty that must be carried out by the Regional Government;
b. that Bitung City as an industrial city that is developing rapidly as one of the economic centers in North Sulawesi Province, has created many job opportunities so that many people from various areas outside Bitung City come to work within the Bitung City area and potentially create social friction which can result in the vulnerability of women and children to become victims of acts of violence;
c. that in the framework of implementing regional autonomy which refers to Article 12 paragraph (2) letter b and Article 236 of Law Number 23 Year 2014 concerning Regional Government, particularly in the field of women's empowerment and child protection which is included in concurrent government affairs that become the authority of Regional Government namely mandatory government affairs not related to basic services, the Region establishes a Regional Regulation;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children from Acts of Violence in Bitung City;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 4 Year 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3143);
3. Law Number 7 Year 1990 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regional Municipality of Bitung (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1990 Number 52, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3421);
4. Law Number 39 Year 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
5. Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235), as has been amended several times most recently by Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 Year 2016 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2016 Number 99, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5882);
