ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 5
(1) Regional Governments are obligated to protect every woman and child in the Region from various types of acts of violence.
(2) Acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) consist of:
a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. neglect; and
e. exploitation.

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE MAYOR OF BITUNG,

Considering : a. that the guarantee of respect, protection and fulfillment of Human Rights for every Indonesian Citizen in the Region is a duty that must be carried out by the Regional Government;
b. that Bitung City as an industrial city that is developing rapidly as one of the economic centers in North Sulawesi Province, has created many job opportunities so that many people from various areas outside Bitung City come to work within the Bitung City area and potentially create social friction which can result in the vulnerability of women and children to become victims of acts of violence;
